--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT WAS BUILT (32 Swift files under TeslaSync/Features/Notifications/)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A native SwiftUI / HIG reproduction of the typed Alert-Rule Studio, bound to an
`@Observable AlertStudioPageModel` driven through the KMP-core seam
`AlertStudioDataSource` (ADR-004). The view body holds no business logic; the
ported web helpers (signal catalog, value-kind resolution, canSave gate,
buildSavePayload, escalation, ruleToEditor, recommendedTriggerMode) live in pure
Foundation files and are unit-proven by the model-logic harness below.

  Models / logic ....... AlertStudioModels, AlertStudioTemplates(+Part1..4),
                         AlertStudioSignals, AlertStudioFormat, AlertStudioValidation,
                         AlertStudioKeys (centralized prompt-key i18n names)
  State holder ......... AlertStudioPageModel(+.Editor/.Derivations/.Mutations/.Draft)
  Seam ................. AlertStudioDataSource(+.Sample)  (hook-named: useAlertRules,
                         useNotificationChannels, useVehicles, useAlertMetrics,
                         useSaveAlertRule, useDeleteAlertRule, useToggleAlertRule,
                         useSnoozeAlertRule, useTestAlertRule, useBulkEnableRules,
                         useBulkDisableRules)  — 11 web hooks, names kept at call sites
  i18n ................. AlertStudioStrings (ASStrings → translation.* catalog)
  Views ................ AlertStudioPage(+ .Templates/.Rules/.RuleRow/.Editor/
                         .EditorOperand/.ValueEditor/.EditorBehavior/.Escalation/
                         .Channels/.Snooze), AlertStudioPrimitives, AlertStudioControls
  Navigation ........... AlertStudioRouteRegistration + AppRoute.notificationsAlertStudio
                         (pathSegment notifications/studio, Operations group) +
                         AppRouteParser alias /notifications/studio + TeslaSyncApp wiring

Live SSE: not applicable — every Alert Studio source is a REST query/mutation, so
no `>2 min` staleness chip is rendered (ADR-013 N/A for this page).
SI units: the page authors raw signal-threshold comparison values in the signal's
native unit (not SI telemetry), so no SI display-boundary conversion is required.
AI sub-features (AINLAlertBuilder, AICrossRuleConflictDetection,
AIAlertTuningSuggestions) and the standalone ComputedMetricEditor / AlertMessageEditor
are separate P4 component parity units (off-baseline by ADR-015 §I3) and are out of
this page's 8-GlassPanel scope; the page reproduces its own panels only.

